PROMPT 5 — ROUTELESS ROUTING ENGINE AND MISSED BUS RESCUE
ROLE

Act as a senior algorithm engineer specializing in graph algorithms and transportation optimization.

Continue the existing ROUTELESS application.

OBJECTIVE

Build a deterministic route calculation engine that works with the project's transportation dataset.

ROUTING MODEL

Represent:

Bus stops as graph nodes.
Bus connections as graph edges.
Travel time as edge weights.
Transfers as additional waiting time.
Road closures as unavailable edges.
Bus status as a route constraint.
Seat availability as an allocation constraint.

Implement Dijkstra's algorithm for earliest-arrival journeys with scheduled departures and transfers.

ROUTE RANKING

Rank routes by:

Safe and operational connections.
Meeting the requested arrival deadline.
Earliest arrival.
Fewest transfers.
Reliable information.
Available capacity.

Return the complete journey:

Boarding stop.
Bus number.
Departure time.
Intermediate stops.
Transfer locations.
Connecting buses.
Final arrival time.
MISSED BUS RESCUE

Build a module called:

MISSED BUS RESCUE — FIND YOUR NEXT BOARDING OPPORTUNITY.

Workflow:

Identify the selected bus as departed.
Retrieve its latest known location.
Identify upcoming authorized stops.
Calculate student travel time to each stop.
Compare possible arrival times.
Include a safety buffer.
Recommend a feasible boarding opportunity.
Otherwise find another route.

Never encourage chasing moving buses or boarding at unauthorized locations.

If GPS data is stale, clearly warn the student.

VALIDATION

Create independent test cases for:

Direct routes.
Multiple transfers.
Waiting time.
Missed connections.
Unavailable buses.
Blocked roads.
Unreachable destinations.
Equal-arrival route tie-breaking.
ACCEPTANCE TESTS
Correct earliest-arrival routes.
No blocked-road recommendations.
No unavailable-bus recommendations.
Correct transfer calculations.
Correct boarding times.
Explicit no-route results.
Missed Bus Rescue provides safe alternatives.

Keep routing independent of UI components and preserve earlier functionality.
